<title>USA: UST Corp Q3 profit sharply higher.</title>
<headline>UST Corp Q3 profit sharply higher.</headline>
<dateline>BOSTON 1996-10-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>1996			1995</p>
<p> Shr			  $0.71		    $0.23</p>
<p> Net			 12,938		    4,145</p>
<p> Avg shrs		  18,217		   18,156</p>
<p>		     Nine Months</p>
<p> Shr			  $1.45		    $0.58</p>
<p> Net			 26,299		   10,459</p>
<p> Avg shrs		  18,179		   18,030</p>
<p>(All Data Above 000s Except Per Share Numbers)</p>
<p>NOTES: 1996 net includes gains of $14.6 million in quarter and $18.6 million reflecting reductions in the loan loss reserve. These compare to 1995 loan loss provisions of $2.8 million and $11.3 million, respectively.</p>
<p>1996 Q3 also includes charge of $3.0 million for  Savings Association Insurance Fund assessment.</p>
<p>-- New York Newsdesk 212-859-1610.</p>
</text>
